title: mf log show
tags: [[CLI command]] [[Event log]]
kind: reference
summary: Show full details of one log context (a log context id, or HEAD for the newest operation's)

One log context — its name, description and ancestors — and its own operations with their values before and after; `--raw` for the JSON ([[Reading the log]]).

A log context with no operation of its own says so instead of stopping after its header: `(empty: no operation)`, or, for a context opened by `mf context new`, the nested log contexts its commands wrote in (`(no operation of its own: see its sub-label 7)`).
